  "body": "Found by the read-only second review of PR #2894 (merged). The finding comes from a read of the code. No run proves it yet.\n\n## What happens\n\nPR #2894 refuses a chamfer with no picked edges when the edge loop is partly bevelled. The check in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs` reads each part of the loop whose plan offset from the wall is more than 0.05 mm as \"bevelled\".\n\nA side with draft also has a plan offset. With a chamfer width of 1 mm and a 90 degree cone, a draft of more than about 3 degrees is above 0.05 mm. Before PR #2894, the chamfer followed that wall, and the result was a valid chamfer. Now the operation is refused, and the message says \"modelled chamfer\", which is not correct for a drafted side.\n\n## Workaround\n\nPick the edges.\n\n## What is expected\n\n- A loop that has a drafted side and no modelled chamfer cuts as before, or\n- the refusal stays, with a message that names the drafted side correctly, and the decision file of #2887 says so.\n\nThe work decides between the two and records the decision.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A test with a plate that has one side drafted more than 3 degrees pins the result.\n- The partly bevelled plate of #2887 is still refused.\n\nRefs #2887\n",
